      "name": "Agent bean lifecycle",
      "summary": "The whole life of a work-plan item, and the rules that make one agent's bean legible to another: check before you create, claim before you work, keep the body current as you go, and end it in a state that says why.",
      "description": "The whole life of a work-plan item, and the rules that make one agent's bean legible to another: check before you create, claim before you work, keep the body current as you go, and end it in a state that says why.\n\nYou are in this process the moment durable work is identified — which is before the first tool call, not after the work is done. The second lane exists because a bean you did not open is not yours to close: coordination replaces a decision you are not entitled to make.\n\nThe one irreversible thing is refused outright. Unwanted work is SCRAPPED with its reasons, never deleted, because a scrapped bean stops the next agent re-entering a dead end while a deleted one leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/bean-lifecycle.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/processes/sdlc/bean-lifecycle.bpmn",
